56 < 2 ### The one A/B difference, explained (not deletion-caused)
57 < 2 
58 < 2 A's overall verdict was NEEDS_ACK where B's was PASS. The acks are two
59 < 2 `deferred:runtime` items A's engine run declared in its workflow report
60 < 2 (plan pins Python 3.11, sandbox had 3.9.6; `ledger/cli.py` never invoked as
61 < 2 a real process). `gate_check.py` — byte-identical on both engines —
62 < 2 faithfully converts report-declared deferrals into acks; B's run declared
63 < 2 none. The divergence is reviewer-judgment variance in report *content*
64 < 2 (the report producer `waves.js` is untouched by the branch), not gate
65 < 2 machinery. n=1 variance, consistent with the 0.1.0 doctrine.
