77 < 2 ## Eval-kit findings (the ceremony's own defects, fixed to get here)
78 < 2 
79 < 2 Three rounds were needed; the first two failed in the *kit*, not the engines
80 < 2 — both engines failed identically each time, so no cell ever produced a
81 < 2 biased comparison.
82 < 2 
83 < 2 1. **#107 follow-up — auth does not ride into a virgin `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`**
84 < 2    ("Not logged in"), and the first remedy — copying
85 < 2    `~/.claude/.credentials.json` into the throwaway — fails once the
86 < 2    operator's live session rotates the refresh token: both cells died with
87 < 2    "OAuth session expired and could not be refreshed" (file was ~21h stale).
88 < 2    **Fix:** export the live credentials from the macOS Keychain
89 < 2    (`security find-generic-password -s "Claude Code-credentials" -w`) at
90 < 2    cell-run time, file copy as fallback. A durable eval-config-isolation
91 < 2    answer must source auth from the Keychain at launch, never from a stored
92 < 2    copy. (For issue #107's closed thread / #122.)
93 < 2 2. **Headless print mode races the SessionStart hook:** the Workflow
94 < 2    engine's saved-workflow registry snapshots before the hook's harness copy
95 < 2    lands, so the probe got `Workflow "ultrapowers-probe" not found` even
96 < 2    though `probe.js` was on disk by end of startup. Interactively the hook
97 < 2    wins this race (why live `/ultrapowers` sessions work); headlessly it
98 < 2    loses. **Fix:** the cell driver pre-seeds the pinned engine's harnesses
99 < 2    into `repo/.claude/workflows/` before any claude process starts, and
100 < 2    mirrors the production gitignore (`.claude/` in `.git/info/exclude`) so
101 < 2    the dirt measurement stays scoped to the deliberately seeded dirt.
102 < 2 
